GOAL
----
Provide all 18 VUMA-required `qemu-<isa>-static` user-mode binaries on $PATH,
each reporting version ≥ 10.0 (caveat §4.2).  Required ISAs:

  aarch64 aarch64_be alpha arm armeb hppa i386 loongarch64 m68k
  mips64 mips64el ppc64 ppc64le riscv32 riscv64 s390x sparc64 x86_64

ENVIRONMENT PROBE
-----------------
- /etc/os-release : Debian GNU/Linux 13 (trixie), amd64
- whoami / id     : z (uid 1001, gid 1001) — non-root
- sudo -n true    : FAILS ("a password is required")  — no passwordless sudo
- which qemu-*    : all MISSING before install (no system qemu-user / qemu)
- dpkg -l | qemu  : (empty)
- apt-cache policy qemu-user-static :
    Candidate: 1:10.0.11+ds-0+deb13u1   (Debian trixie/main)  ← ≥ 10.0 ✅
    Also:     1:10.0.2+ds-2+deb13u1    (trixie-security)

PATH CHOSEN
-----------
`apt-get install` is blocked by the dpkg lock (no root).  Fall back to plan
(b) of the protocol: download the .deb files via `apt-get download` (which
needs no root) and extract them locally into $HOME/.local/bin.

Debian 13's `qemu-user-static` package is now transitional: it ships only
`qemu-<isa>-static -> qemu-<isa>` SYMLINKS, with the actual binaries in the
`qemu-user` package.  Therefore both packages were downloaded:

  apt-get download qemu-user-static    -> 70 KB  (symlinks only)
  apt-get download qemu-user           -> 71 MB  (real binaries)

Both at version 1:10.0.11+ds-0+deb13u1.

INSTALLATION STEPS
------------------
1. mkdir -p $HOME/.local/bin
2. dpkg-deb -x qemu-user_*.deb /tmp/qemu-extract
3. Copied the 18 required real binaries `qemu-<isa>` from
   /tmp/qemu-extract/usr/bin/ to $HOME/.local/bin/  (chmod 0755).
4. Created `qemu-<isa>-static -> qemu-<isa>` symlinks in $HOME/.local/bin/
   for each of the 18 required ISAs (mirrors Debian qemu-user-static).
5. Also created the compat aliases the upstream deb ships:
   qemu-amd64->qemu-x86_64, qemu-arm64->qemu-aarch64,
   qemu-loong64->qemu-loongarch64, qemu-powerpc->qemu-ppc,
   qemu-armel->qemu-arm, qemu-armhf->qemu-arm, qemu-ppc64el->qemu-ppc64le.
6. Appended an idempotent PATH-prepend block for $HOME/.local/bin to both
   ~/.bashrc and ~/.profile (so fresh login shells find qemu-* unaided).
7. Wrote vuma/scripts/env/qemu-env.sh — a small `source`-able wrapper that
   prepends $HOME/.local/bin to PATH idempotently, for non-login shells
   (CI, bash -c).  Mirrors the z3-env.sh / rust-env.sh convention.

NATURE OF THE BINARIES
----------------------
`file $HOME/.local/bin/qemu-x86_64` reports:
  ELF 64-bit LSB pie executable, x86-64, version 1 (GNU/Linux),
  static-pie linked, stripped
`ldd` reports: "statically linked".

So the binaries ARE genuinely statically linked (static-PIE), even though
upstream names them `qemu-<isa>` rather than `qemu-<isa>-static`.  The
`-static` symlinks satisfy the VUMA test-suite's expected names directly;
no DoD "non-static fallback" branch was needed.

